{"source":"github","project_id":"itdepends","target":"r-lib/itdepends","id":"issue/26","ref":26,"title":"as.tibble -\u003e as_tibble","description":"Thanks for this package! When running `dep_usage_pkg`, I get the following warning:\r\n\r\n```r\r\n`as.tibble()` was deprecated in tibble 2.0.0.\r\nℹ Please use `as_tibble()` instead.\r\nℹ The signature and semantics have changed, see `?as_tibble`.\r\nℹ The deprecated feature was likely used in the itdepends package.\r\n  Please report the issue to the authors.\r\n```","published_at":"2022-12-28T20:51:14Z","url":"https://github.com/r-lib/itdepends/issues/26","type":"issue","extra":{"author":"LukasWallrich","state":"OPEN"}}
{"source":"github","project_id":"itdepends","target":"r-lib/itdepends","id":"issue/27","ref":27,"title":"Change README install repo","description":"In the readme the install address is wrong:\r\n\r\n```r\r\n# install.packages(\"devtools\")\r\ndevtools::install_github(\"jimhester/itdepends\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nShould be:\r\n```r\r\n# install.packages(\"devtools\")\r\nremotes::install_github(\"r-lib/itdepends\")\r\n```","published_at":"2023-05-19T20:47:19Z","url":"https://github.com/r-lib/itdepends/issues/27","type":"issue","extra":{"author":"phisanti","state":"OPEN"}}
{"source":"github","project_id":"itdepends","target":"r-lib/itdepends","id":"issue/25","ref":25,"title":"Move `master` branch to `main`","description":"The `master` branch of this repository will soon be renamed to `main`, as part of a coordinated change across several GitHub organizations (including, but not limited to: [tidyverse](https://github.com/tidyverse), [r-lib](https://github.com/r-lib), [tidymodels](https://github.com/tidymodels), and [sol-eng](https://github.com/sol-eng)). We anticipate this will happen by the end of September 2021.\n\nThat will be preceded by a release of the [usethis package](https://usethis.r-lib.org), which will gain some functionality around detecting and adapting to a renamed default branch. There will also be a blog post at the time of this `master` --\u003e `main` change.\n\nThe purpose of this issue is to:\n\n* Help us firm up the list of targetted repositories\n* Make sure all maintainers are aware of what's coming\n* Give us an issue to close when the job is done\n* Give us a place to put advice for collaborators re: how to adapt\n\n*message id: euphoric_snowdog*\n","published_at":"2021-09-08T01:38:09Z","updated_at":"2021-10-27T22:32:22Z","url":"https://github.com/r-lib/itdepends/issues/25","type":"issue","extra":{"author":"jennybc","state":"CLOSED"}}
{"source":"github","project_id":"itdepends","target":"r-lib/itdepends","id":"issue/23","ref":23,"title":"\"Could not load or update metadata cache\" (HTTP 404)","description":"Is `itdepends` still an actively developed package or was this more of a proof of principle?  \r\n\r\nIt's not precisely clear where the compile timing stats are coming from, is this something `itdepends` is supposed to be computing on the fly/from local cache? It seems to be trying to access a remote resource for this information, unsuccessfully.  \r\n\r\n\r\n```r\r\nitdepends::dep_weight(\"itdepends\")\r\nx Metadata update failed                                      \r\nGarbage collection 321 = 230+16+75 (level 0) ... \r\n137.7 Mbytes of cons cells used (65%)\r\n112.0 Mbytes of vectors used (68%)\r\nError in stop(http_error(resp)) : \r\nNot Found (HTTP 404).\r\n\r\nCould not load or update metadata cache. If you think your local cache is broken, try deleting it with `meta_cache_cleanup()`, or the `$cleanup()` method.\r\n\r\nEnter a frame number, or 0 to exit   \r\n\r\n1: itdepends::dep_weight(\"itdepends\")\r\n2: vapply(user_deps, function(x) sum(bin_size(x), na.rm = TRUE), numeric(1))\r\n3: FUN(X[[i]], ...)\r\n4: bin_size(x)\r\n5: cache$list(pkgs)\r\n6: synchronise(self$async_list(packages))\r\n```","published_at":"2020-06-04T20:01:18Z","url":"https://github.com/r-lib/itdepends/issues/23","type":"issue","extra":{"author":"cboettig","state":"OPEN"}}
{"source":"github","project_id":"itdepends","target":"r-lib/itdepends","id":"issue/15","ref":15,"title":"Condition length problem (?)","description":"Discovered incidentally while rendering the tidyverse.org site. Things came to a halt on the itdepends post.\r\n\r\nRe-running the code manually, I see:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\u003e weights \u003c- itdepends::dep_weight(c(\"dplyr\", \"data.table\"))\r\nError in !is.na(match) \u0026\u0026 match[1] == 1 : \r\n'length(x) = 2 \u003e 1' in coercion to 'logical(1)'\r\n\r\nCould not load or update metadata cache. If you think your local cache is\r\nbroken, try deleting it with `meta_cache_cleanup()`, or the `$cleanup()`\r\nmethod.\r\nIn addition: Warning message:\r\nUnquoting language objects with `!!!` is deprecated as of rlang 0.4.0.\r\nPlease use `!!` instead.\r\n\r\n  # Bad:\r\n  dplyr::select(data, !!!enquo(x))\r\n\r\n  # Good:\r\n  dplyr::select(data, !!enquo(x))    # Unquote single quosure\r\n  dplyr::select(data, !!!enquos(x))  # Splice list of quosures\r\n```","published_at":"2019-07-04T16:19:56Z","updated_at":"2020-04-03T14:51:30Z","url":"https://github.com/r-lib/itdepends/issues/15","type":"issue","extra":{"author":"jennybc","state":"CLOSED"}}
{"source":"github","project_id":"itdepends","target":"r-lib/itdepends","id":"issue/11","ref":11,"title":"Error: $ operator is invalid for atomic vectors  in itdepends::dep_usage_proj","description":"Hi there!\r\n\r\nThanks so much for the cool package, it works great for packages!\r\n\r\nI ran into some issues with getting `itdepends::dep_usage_proj()` to work for projects, I generally don't get much further than this:\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- language-all: lang-r --\u003e\r\n\r\n    itdepends::dep_usage_proj()\r\n    #\u003e Error: $ operator is invalid for atomic vectors\r\n\r\n\u003csup\u003eCreated on 2019-02-06 by the [reprex package](https://reprex.tidyverse.org) (v0.2.1)\u003c/sup\u003e\r\n\r\nAny ideas on how I can resolve this?\r\n\r\nThanks so much in advance for any pointers!","published_at":"2019-02-06T08:54:02Z","url":"https://github.com/r-lib/itdepends/issues/11","tags":["bug"],"type":"issue","extra":{"author":"balthasars","state":"OPEN"}}
